  "review_corrections": [
    {
      "id": "REI-R106-01",
      "change": "Removed the per-case cosmic_age_at_mean_z20_s_from_locked_background and cosmic_age_at_restart_s fields and the a=1e-12..a_ref quadrature of the sheared H law that produced them (outside the locked domain; SCENARIO_LOCK clock.absolute_cosmic_age_s=null). Added one top-level q=0 FLRW age at zbar=20, labelled EXTERNAL_CONVENTION_OUTSIDE_LOCKED_DOMAIN and identical for all cases. No q-dependent extrapolated age is reported. The z<4 foreground H model is now labelled as an extension beyond a_end (sensitivity only)."
    },
    {
      "id": "REI-R106-02",
      "change": "Provenance is described as RECEIPT_LINKED_PLUS_CONTENT_BOUND for the four composed cases and GIT_MANIFEST_HASH_BOUND_PLUS_CONTENT_BOUND for SHEAR_PLUS. COMPOSITION_RECEIPT.json, composed RETURN.txt and composed checkpoint.txt are hashed into input_sha256. chain_ok now also requires equality of every RETURN counter/clock/error field with the checkpoint and of both RETURN residuals with the natively recomputed residuals. The git refs whose tips actually contain each checkpoint sha256 are found by a scan of the rei_bianchi object store run now, and the REI_COMMIT ancestry is recorded."
    },
    {
      "id": "REI-R106-03",
      "change": "The dt-form versus dN-form agreement is reported as a clock/H consistency check (dt/dN=1/H) plus a quadrature-error estimate (native rows versus Richardson and versus a cubic spline). It is stated not to validate tau(4..20), because both forms share n_e, sigma_T and H."
    },
    {
      "id": "REI-R106-04",
      "change": "Renamed ne_vs_native_eos_cm3, ne_vs_history_last_row_cm3 and abundance_rows_charge_neutrality_cm3 to electron_formula_*_consistency fields, and stated that charge neutrality is imposed by the EOS (n_e = n_H x_HII + n_He (x_HeII + 2 x_HeIII)); these are bookkeeping identities, not tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "REI-R106-05",
      "change": "The z<4 list is now a top-level z_below_4_continuation with three independent blockers (1 scenario-lock scope, 2 DriverConfig::validate 4<=end_zbar<20, 3 source redshift guard plus no admitted z<4 source model), each with the source line found now in both compiled epochs, and with background domain, absolute age and stored H/s marked DERIVED or NON_BLOCKING. Each case records the positive control from the cached native replay: the config.cfg end_zbar passed DriverConfig::read and Driver::new (both call validate)."
    },
    {
      "id": "REI-R106-06",
      "change": "Each case states the replay window next to the residual: accepted-step count, zbar range, rejections in window, attempts per step and the per-step dln a regime (constant step, endpoint-clipped final step). The headline residual covers every compared field including ledgers, photons and the energy residual. The reject and step-size-change branches are listed as not exercised. No new native window run."
    },
